  "user_handle": "slavina",
  "body": "I already submitted this vulnerability, but I didn't read the `readme.md`, so the PoC I uploaded for the previous issue does not work if copy-pasted into `C4PoC.t.sol`. So this is the same issue, but with the correct PoC. Sorry for the trouble.\n\n## Finding description and impact\n\nMerkl allows creators to override campaign parameters, with some limitations: creators cannot change the start timestamp of the campaign if it already started, and they cannot set the end timestamp to a time in the past.\n```solidity\nfunction overrideCampaign(bytes32 _campaignId, CampaignParameters memory newCampaign) external {\n    CampaignParameters memory _campaign = campaign(_campaignId);\n    _isValidOperator(_campaign.creator);\n    if (\n        // ...\n        (newCampaign.startTimestamp != _campaign.startTimestamp && block.timestamp > _campaign.startTimestamp) || // Allow to update startTimestamp before campaign start\n        // End timestamp should be in the future\n        newCampaign.duration + _campaign.startTimestamp <= block.timestamp\n    ) revert Errors.InvalidOverride();\n\n    // ...\n    campaignOverrides[_campaignId] = newCampaign;\n    // ...\n}\n```\nBut when checking these constraints, the function `overrideCampaign` uses the initial campaign(`_campaign` which comes from `_campaignLookup[_campaignId]`) as a reference point for the start time, instead of the most recent compaign(`campaignOverrides[_campaignId]`).\n```solidity\nfunction campaign(bytes32 _campaignId) public view returns (CampaignParameters memory) {\n    return campaignList[campaignLookup(_campaignId)];\n}\n\nfunction campaignLookup(bytes32 _campaignId) public view returns (uint256) {\n    uint256 index = _campaignLookup[_campaignId];\n    if (index == 0) revert Errors.CampaignDoesNotExist();\n    return index - 1;\n}\n```\nSo in the case in which a creator postpones a campaign, and then, for whatever reason, they decide to postpone it again, they are not allowed to do so if they do it after what was the initial start timestamp.\n\n## Vulnerable scenarios\n\n1. creator sets up a campaign with start time x\ncreator overrides the campaign and sets its start time to y\ncreator tries to override the campaign at a time after x but before y, but can't, even though they should\n\n2. creator sets up a campaign with start time x\ncreator overrides the campaign and sets its start time to y\ncreator tries to override the campaign and set its duration to a time that if added to y is in the future, but added to x is in the past, but can't, even though they should\n\n## Impact\n\nUsers of Merkl are unable to access some Merkl functionalities. The inability to postpone or cut the duration of a campaign could make Merkl users unsatisfied with the protocol, and it can cause problems for them because the campaign may not proceed in the ways they had intended it to go.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\n\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport { Fixture } from \"../Fixture.t.sol\";\nimport { CampaignParameters } from \"../../contracts/DistributionCreator.sol\";\nimport { Errors } from \"../../contracts/utils/Errors.sol\";\n\ncontract C4PoC is Fixture {\n    uint256 internal constant maxDistribForOOG = 1e4;\n    uint256 internal constant nbrDistrib = 10;\n    uint32 internal initStartTime;\n    uint32 internal initEndTime;\n    uint32 internal startTime;\n    uint32 internal endTime;\n    uint32 internal numEpoch;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        initStartTime = uint32(block.timestamp);\n        numEpoch = 25;\n        initEndTime = startTime + numEpoch * EPOCH_DURATION;\n\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        creator.setFeeRecipient(dylan);\n\n        vm.startPrank(guardian);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        tokens[0] = address(angle);\n        amounts[0] = 1e8;\n        creator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        angle.mint(address(alice), 1e22);\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        angle.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        uint256 amount = 100 ether;\n        uint256 amountAfterFees = 90 ether;\n        uint32 startTimestamp_initial = 500_000;\n\n        bytes memory campaignData = abi.encode(\n            0xbEEfa1aBfEbE621DF50ceaEF9f54FdB73648c92C,\n            new address[](0),\n            new address[](0),\n            \"\",\n            new bytes[](0),\n            new bytes[](0),\n            hex\"\"\n        );\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        bytes32 campaignId = creator.createCampaign(\n            CampaignParameters({\n                campaignId: bytes32(0),\n                creator: alice,\n                rewardToken: address(angle),\n                amount: amount,\n                campaignType: 1,\n                startTimestamp: startTimestamp_initial,\n                duration: 1_000_000,\n                campaignData: campaignData\n            })\n        );\n\n        uint32 startTimestamp_1 = 1_000_000;\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        creator.overrideCampaign(\n            campaignId,\n            CampaignParameters({\n                campaignId: campaignId,\n                creator: alice,\n                rewardToken: address(angle),\n                amount: amountAfterFees,\n                campaignType: 1,\n                startTimestamp: startTimestamp_1,\n                duration: 1_000_000,\n                campaignData: campaignData\n            })\n        );\n\n        // we are now after the initial startTimestamp but before the current one\n        vm.warp(750_000);\n\n        uint32 startTimestamp_2 = uint32(1_500_000);\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        vm.expectRevert(Errors.InvalidOverride.selector);\n        creator.overrideCampaign(\n            campaignId,\n            CampaignParameters({\n                campaignId: campaignId,\n                creator: alice,\n                rewardToken: address(angle),\n                amount: amountAfterFees,\n                campaignType: 1,\n                startTimestamp: startTimestamp_2,\n                duration: 1_000_000,\n                campaignData: campaignData\n            })\n        );\n\n        // end time in the future if you apply duration_override to startTimestamp_1,\n        // but in the past if you apply it to startTimestamp_initial\n        uint32 duration_override = 200_000;\n        \n        vm.prank(alice);\n        vm.expectRevert(Errors.InvalidOverride.selector);\n        creator.overrideCampaign(\n            campaignId,\n            CampaignParameters({\n                campaignId: campaignId,\n                creator: alice,\n                rewardToken: address(angle),\n                amount: amountAfterFees,\n                campaignType: 1,\n                startTimestamp: startTimestamp_1,\n                duration: duration_override,\n                campaignData: campaignData\n            })\n        );\n    }\n}\n```",
